      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "τῶν γὰρ τὸν οὐρανὸν ἐνοικούντων πνευμάτων",
          "english_quote": "Among the spirits inhabiting heaven",
          "issue": "The opening omits γάρ's explicit explanatory connection: the angels' intervention explains the punishment introduced in 8.11. The clause itself is covered, but its marked discourse relationship is weakened.",
          "suggested_revision": "Begin “For, among the spirits inhabiting heaven, ...” or use another explicit explanatory connective. Submit the revised wording for fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "reference": "8.13",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": false,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "lexical_fidelity": false,
        "uncertainties_disclosed": false
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "τὰ ἐκ πυρὸς τραπέντα μέλη εἰς τὸ πρῶτον αὐτῶν τῆς ἰδίας φύσεως ἀμίαντον· μετασυγκρῖναι οὐκ ἐξίσχυσαν.",
          "english_quote": "they were not strong enough to recombine the members that had been transformed from fire into the original, undefiled state of their own nature.",
          "issue": "The English readily attaches “into the original, undefiled state” to “had been transformed from fire,” suggesting that the earlier transformation already returned the limbs to their original condition. The intended restoration belongs to μετασυγκρῖναι, whose accomplishment is negated. The note explains the intended attachment, but the main sentence should make it clear.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider “they were not strong enough to recombine their limbs, which had been transformed from fire, into the original undefiled state of their own nature.” Preserve and disclose the supplied punctuation rather than treating it as an OCR error. This proposed wording requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "τῷ γὰρ βάρει τῷ ὑπὸ τῆς ἐπιθυμίας εἰς σάρκα τελευτήσαντος αὐτῶν τοῦ πυρός, τὴν ἀσεβοῦσαν ὥδευσαν ὁδὸν κάτω·",
          "english_quote": "For under the weight produced by desire, their fire ended in flesh, and they traveled the impious road downward.",
          "issue": "The Greek makes the fire's ending in flesh a genitive participial qualification of the fire whose weight bears them downward. The draft instead makes that transformation an independent event occurring “under the weight,” thereby introducing an unsupported causal arrangement. The note reinforces this rearrangement by saying that the weight causes the fiery nature to terminate in flesh. Merely listing a better attachment as an alternative does not support the chosen main wording.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider “For, under the weight of their fire, which through desire had ended in flesh, they traveled the impious road downward.” Revise the note to distinguish the transformation through desire from the weight associated with the resulting flesh. Any alternative attachment must still preserve the genitive qualification of τοῦ πυρός and the dative phrase's relationship to ὥδευσαν. Review the replacement afresh.",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "reference": "8.14",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": true,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "lexical_fidelity": false,
        "uncertainties_disclosed": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "μετὰ γὰρ συνουσίαν",
          "english_quote": "After intercourse",
          "issue": "The temporal phrase is translated, but γάρ's explanatory force is omitted. This section elaborates the consequences of the loss of transformative power described in 8.13; the draft presents it only as the next chronological development.",
          "suggested_revision": "Begin “For after intercourse, ...” or otherwise retain the explicit explanatory connection. The proposed change requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "reference": "8.15",
      "verdict": "blocked",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": false,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "lexical_fidelity": false,
        "uncertainties_disclosed": false
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "μάννα αὐτοῖς ὁ παντοδύναμος θεὸς ἐπώμβρισεν ἐκ ποικίλης ἐπιθυμίας",
          "english_quote": "almighty God rained down upon them manna suited to every variety of desire",
          "issue": "The following enjoyment clause supports a contextual rendering in which the manna answers varied appetites, so this choice is not inherently blocking. However, the note does not preserve the material causal alternative for ἐκ ποικίλης ἐπιθυμίας: the varied appetite can explain why the manna was supplied rather than directly describe its properties. “Suited to every variety” also makes that contextual inference more explicit than the Greek phrase itself.",
          "suggested_revision": "Either retain the contextual choice with an explicit alternative such as “because of their varied appetite” and explain the preference, or consider the more source-transparent “almighty God rained manna down upon them in response to their varied desires.” Review any revised wording afresh.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "οἱ δ’ ὑπὸ νόθου φύσεως τῷ καθαρῷ τῆς τροφῆς οὐκ ἀρεσκόμενοι, μόνης τῆς τῶν αἱμάτων γεύσεως ἐγλίχοντα.",
          "english_quote": "But because of their illegitimate nature, they were not pleased with the purity of the food and craved only the taste of blood.",
          "issue": "The printed ἐγλίχοντα does not supply an established finite plural form agreeing with οἱ in this construction. “Craved” depends on treating it as the conjecturally corrected ἐγλίχοντο. The draft's source_issues correctly discloses that dependence, but disclosure does not establish the main rendering from the supplied reading. The image-checked transcription verifies the printed form; the unresolved problem is its grammatical account or an evidenced correction, not an unverified OCR reading.",
          "suggested_revision": "Keep the publication block unless a defensible linguistic account of printed ἐγλίχοντα is established, or textual evidence and an explicit editorial decision support the proposed correction ἐγλίχοντο. Continue distinguishing that proposed correction from the supplied reading. Any resulting English must undergo fresh review; do not present the conjectural finite rendering as already accepted.",
          "severity": "blocking"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
